X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Meetup Group Ohazunav": "https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-ohazunav/events/315319846/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_meetup_group_ohazunav
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Petaluma Social
UID:event_315319846@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260623T041453Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T163600
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260730T191300
SUMMARY:Shiloh Hike + Picnic Dinner | 4 mi\, 626 ft gain
DESCRIPTION:Mindfull Hikes\n***Please be in good enough shape to hike at a
  moderate/fast steady pace (+/-2.5 mph) and comfortable with elevation cha
 nges.***\n\n**Distance:** +/- 4 miles\n**The hike:** Join me for an aftern
 oon hike and picnic dinner at Shiloh Ranch Regional Park. A loop hike on C
 reekside\, Pond\, Canyon and Big Leaf trails. We'll hike\, eat mid point a
 nd hike back to the start.\n\n**Parking:** Park in the lot for $8 or free 
 if you have a regional park pass.\n\n**Where to meet:** By the Bocce court
  (near entrance) at Shiloh Ranch.\n\n*Please be on time. We’ll start pro
 mptly at the start time listed.* Give yourself a little extra time to arri
 ve and get situated so that you’re part of the opening circle as this is
  an essential part of our time together.\n\n**Restroom:** At Trailhead\n\n
 **What to bring:** Your dinner\, water\, hat\, good hiking shoes\, a joyfu
 l spirit and laughter. Please dress appropriately for the weather that day
 . Layers of clothing are always advisable.\n**============================
 =======**\n**Reminders:**\nMindful hikes are intended to be a way to conne
 ct more fully with ourselves\, each other and with the land. There will be
  two periods of silent walking throughout the hike to allow the senses to 
 be fully alive and felt. There will also be time during the hike to visit 
 and connect with each other. These times of talking and connecting are an 
 invitation to bring mindfulness to the present moment. **It's a time to pu
 t away the cell phone and cameras to disengage from technology to be fully
  present with each other\, our *senses and the land we are inhabiting.***\
 n\n***If you're on the waitlist for the hike and want to attend please mes
 sage Vickie a few days before the scheduled hike. Most hikes have people d
 rop off at the last minute and it's possible there is an opening.***\n\n**
 Dāna**\nIn the spirit of the Buddhist tradition mindful hikes are offered
  as a dāna based event. Rick Hansen says “generosity is a beautiful pra
 ctice that opens and gladdens the heart\, relaxes the contraction of ‘se
 lf’ and ripples out into the world to touch many people.” The dāna pr
 actice is **heart centered** and in the spirit of generosity. Venmo or cas
 h is graciously accepted. Venmo account is: @vickieix8\; last four digits 
 4714 of my phone # if asked.\n\n**No-Show Policy:** Please cancel at least
  24 hours before the start of the hike. Be mindful that there may be a wai
 tlist. If your plans change and you're not coming\, opening up a spot 4-5 
 days before the hike it's more likely someone will be able to attend than 
 if you cancel at the last minute. You're considered a no-show if you cance
 l at the last minute. Members with 2 no-shows are removed from the group.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-ohazunav/events/31531984
 6/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260618T214209Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260618T214209Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
